Just wanted to drop this here in case you guys were interested in what Preact did before switching to the Promise method:

https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/6954d7549f35b5c32421c6855ee29ffda01137d1

```js
let ch;
try { ch = new MessageChannel(); } catch (e) {}
export const defer = ch ? ( f => {
  ch.port1.onmessage = f;
  ch.port2.postMessage('');
}) : setTimeout;
```

AFAIK this had worse browser support than Promise, the runtime performance was slightly worse, and it swallowed errors.  Promise falling back to setTimeout is a great option.
